# ⚠️ DEEP LINKS ARE NOT HANDLED HERE ANY MORE — SEE `worker/index.ts`.
#
# `/i/*`, `/e/*`, `/c/*`, `/u/*` and `/r/*` used to be 200 rewrites onto `go.html` /
# `invite.html`. Cloudflare Workers static assets does not serve a 200 rewrite in place: it
# answers with a 307 to the canonical asset URL, and that redirect DROPS the original path and
# query string. Both pages read exactly what was being dropped — the invite code, and the
# path segment `go.html` uses to name the link — so every shared invite landed on "Ask your
# friend for their code" and Android invite attribution never happened at all.
#
# The `?code=:splat` form could never have worked either: Cloudflare's `_redirects`
# documentation lists query parameters as unsupported — a static query string in a
# destination is fine, a captured `:splat` inside one is not.
#
# ⚠️ DO NOT ADD THOSE PREFIXES BACK. Static assets (this file included) are evaluated BEFORE
# the Worker, so a rule here would redirect the request away before the fix can run.

# `/x/<slug>` is a genuine directory index, so it needs no path to survive and a plain
# rewrite is still correct.
/x/* /competition/ 200
